{
  "dom_id": "step-q117186",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195146/assets/ebb60aa69c324ef1bfc70bc325ff71eca70426225859350c4bbd8a58a82a2757.png)\n\nThe parking lot in a market has a rectangular form whose dimensions are shown in the figure above. What is the area of the parking lot?",
  "worked_solution": "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\nA=a\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na=200\\,m,\\,b=60\\,m.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,  the area of the field is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b=200\\cdot 60=12\\,000\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
